{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TSbmrg8t34HrRynAhMSZ4Q","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-587\"\n3\ttitle = \"LLR-207/TC-205 return: two Detail clauses contradict kitlib/verdict.py, two stated guards have no detector, one TC Method misstates its own fixture, and the CMP-006 note this row falsifies\"\n4\tworkstream = \"process\"\n5\tspecref = \"\"\n6\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n7\tpriority = 2\n8\tsafety_class = \"spine\"\n9\tbar = \"DevStg-Tests\"\n10\t+++\n11\t\n12\t## Deliverable\n13\t\n14\tALL SEVEN findings driven, over three cells and two new regressions.\n15\t`kitlib/verdict.py` is BYTE-IDENTICAL to its pre-lane state (`git diff` over the\n16\tmodule against the integration base is empty) — the return was about text that\n17\tcontradicts the module and guards no fixture drove, and the row asked for no\n18\tbehaviour change.\n19\t\n20\tTHE TWO `LLR-207.detail` CLAUSES now say what the module does, re-driven against\n21\tit rather than inherited. `governing_identity` reads \"the branch tip or an\n22\texplicit revision\" and states that the branch argument is a branch NAME, for the\n23\treason `format_branch_trailer` gives verbatim (`verdict.py:738-740`) — the peel\n24\tverifies a refresh commit against the branch it names, and no refresh subject\n25\tnames `HEAD`. `governing_rev`'s \"until it can peel\" is gone: the peel re-seats\n26\t`rev` and `continue`s (`:465-468`), the walk ends at the first commit whose\n27\tidentity differs from its parent's (`:473`) or at the absent-parent /\n28\t`_MAX_GOVERNING_WALK` bounds, and the clause now says a branch with no refresh\n29\tunder it still walks — which is the OI-76 fix a literal reading of the old\n30\tsentence would have undone.\n31\t\n32\tTHE TWO STATED GUARDS GREW DETECTORS, and both were MUTATION-DRIVEN, because a\n33\tregression that never fails is not one. Each mutation was re-driven AT THE\n34\tCLOSING TIP on a detached `git worktree`, so the run proving the regression could\n35\tleave no residue in the tree being closed:\n36\t- `test_two_logs_at_one_key_declaring_two_phases_serve_no_round` — relaxing the\n37\t  `len(ph) == 1` ambiguity rule (`:608`) to last-wins fails exactly this test and\n38\t  nothing else (`1 failed, 52 passed`).\n39\t- `test_an_attestation_riding_a_commit_that_changed_the_work_is_not_read` —\n40\t  deleting the `governing_identity(...) != tree` carrier guard (`:802-803`) fails\n41\t  exactly this test and nothing else (`1 failed, 52 passed`).\n42\tBoth previously left `134 passed` across the three modules the return measured.\n43\tEach fixture asserts its own premises (both logs really committed, the round file\n44\tstill present; the forged carrier really moved the governing identity) so the\n45\tempty answer is the RULE and not an empty scan.\n46\t\n47\tTHE TWO `TC-205` CELLS. `evidence` now reaches `work_tip` /\n48\t`refresh_attestation`'s refusal arms by citing the five\n49\t`tests/test_integrate_station.py` tests that hold them — all five verified to\n50\texist — with a `Method` sentence saying which arms those are and why the station\n51\tsuite is where they live. `method`'s identity sentence was made true BY THE\n52\tFIXTURE rather than by weakening the sentence: the changed `docs/work/` spec blob\n53\tnow really folds DIFFERENT, the pre-existing dropped-entry assertion left beside\n54\tit as the weaker claim.\n55\t\n56\t`CMP-006`'s note re-points to name BOTH modules not owned there — `station.py`\n57\t(LLR-182, IF-093) and `verdict.py` (LLR-207, IF-175) — the sentence THIS row\n58\tfalsified by giving `verdict.py` a CMP-008 tag. Re-derived at close by the\n59\tcomplementary route (enumerating rows by `Module` path, not by component, checked\n60\tagainst the directory listing): all eleven `kitlib/` modules are claimed by an\n61\tLLR row, and exactly two sit at CMP-008.\n62\t\n63\tSPOTTED, NOT FIXED — the same cell's parenthetical enumerating kitlib's CMP-006\n64\tmembers omits `evi